Copyright (c) Ecoma

This document licenses the source code of Ecoma. It is a fair-code licence:
the source is public, and you may read it, self-host it and modify it. It is
not an OSI open-source licence, and Ecoma is never described as "open source".
The one freedom it withholds is the one an OSI licence cannot withhold —
selling Ecoma itself as a service. That restriction is why the rest can be
open.


SCOPE

These terms cover the files in this repository, with four exceptions. Each
exception is a path, deliberately not a filename marker, so the boundary a
reader checks is the same one the build enforces: every project declares a
`license:*` tag that must agree with its own directory, and
`dev-cli check-project-conventions` fails the build when it does not.

  1. Any directory named `packages` directly beneath a subsystem root — the
     interfaces, schemas, protocols, clients and vocabularies a third party
     needs in order to PLUG INTO Ecoma — is licensed under the Apache License
     2.0, whose text ships in that directory. Nothing in this document limits
     those files.

  2. Any directory named `enterprise` directly beneath a subsystem root is NOT
     licensed by this document. Those files are published so they can be read
     and audited, but using them requires a separate written Enterprise
     License from Ecoma. Their own terms ship in that directory.

  3. The prose under `shared/libs/doctrine/` is licensed under Creative
     Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International; see the LICENSE file in
     that directory. This document covers the source code beside it, not the
     documents.

  4. The `cloud/` directory is proprietary and is not published. If it is
     present in your working tree, it is not licensed by this document and no
     rights to it are granted here.


